# Map frame

Surface and ensemble maps stay inside the named domain (`wide`, `pnw`, or `ca`). Never let a coastline, border, or overlay change the axes.

- Call `ax.set_autoscale_on(False)` and set xlim/ylim to that domain before drawing anything on top of the field.
- `add_boundaries` must plot with `scalex=False, scaley=False`.
- Outline points outside the domain are NaN. Do not draw a full Natural Earth ring, and do not paint Earth Engine country lines (`USDOS/LSIB`) onto thumbnails. That layer drew a false 40°N line.
- After a frame change, recook the affected region and check one image: the latitude span stays the domain span, not the whole world.
- `test_cook.py` asserts California boundaries do not zoom the axes. Do not delete that check.
